From: cezanne port
Subject: [PATCH] st/theme: index the selectors of a stylesheet

add_matched_properties() tested every selector of every stylesheet for
each theme node (~1400 rules with the shell theme and an extension like
dash-to-dock): most of the time St spent styling actors shown for the
first time, e.g. the first open of a menu after a shell start. Selectors
are now filed under what their rightmost simple selector requires of a
node (id, else first class, else element type name), and a node is
tested only against its candidates, in stylesheet order, with the same
matching code: the cascade is unchanged. The index lives with the
CRStyleSheet and is freed with it.
---
diff --git a/src/st/croco/cr-stylesheet.c b/src/st/croco/cr-stylesheet.c
--- a/src/st/croco/cr-stylesheet.c
+++ b/src/st/croco/cr-stylesheet.c
@@ -169,6 +169,8 @@
 {
         g_return_if_fail (a_this);
 
+        if (a_this->st_index && a_this->st_index_free)
+                a_this->st_index_free (a_this->st_index);
         if (a_this->statements) {
                 cr_statement_destroy (a_this->statements);
                 a_this->statements = NULL;
